// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Pharmacy — dispensing (PI-7)
//
// ⚠️ PHARMACY OWNS NO QUANTITY, NO RATE AND NO CLINICAL CONTENT. It is a
//   WORKFLOW over product + inventory + regulatory. Quantity lives in
//   `stock_ledger` and is only ever moved by `recordMovement()` (PI-ADR-004);
//   price and tax live in the invoice engine and are reached through a charge
//   request in PI-8, never by inserting an invoice line here (PI-ADR-005/006);
//   the clinical content of a prescription lives in `encounter_prescriptions`
//   and is READ.
//
// ⚠️ INVARIANT 7: READING A PATIENT'S RECORD IS NOT WRITING IN IT. Nothing in
//   this file writes a prescription, amends one, or carries a column that could
//   be mistaken for one. `dispense_lines.encounter_prescription_id` is a
//   foreign key INTO the clinical record and the arrow points one way. A
//   pharmacist who needs a prescription changed asks the prescriber; that is a
//   workflow, not a permission.
//
// ── WHY A DISPENSE HAS NO DRAFT STATE ────────────────────────────────────────
// Every other document in this programme drafts, then posts: a purchase order
// is written, checked and issued. A dispense does not, because the physical act
// and the record are the same event — the medicine leaves the shelf and goes
// into somebody's hand once, and a draft dispense would be stock that has left
// the building with no ledger row saying so. So the workspace assembles a PLAN
// (`inventory/allocation.service.ts`, which writes nothing), a human confirms
// it, and ONE transaction writes the dispense, its allocations, its ledger legs
// and its regulatory snapshot. A refusal at any point leaves nothing behind and
// burns no number.
//
// The verification step that other documents get from a draft lives on
// `prescription_fulfilments` instead, one step earlier and against the
// PRESCRIPTION rather than against the supply.
//
// ── PHI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ⚠️ THIS IS THE MOST PHI-DENSE TABLE GROUP IN THE PROGRAMME. "This person was
//   given this medicine on this day" is a clinical fact about a named human,
//   and three columns below are marked accordingly. Nothing here may be logged,
//   cached in Redis, or put in a URL. `data_access_logs` records that a
//   dispense was READ, with ids and counts — never a medicine name and never a
//   patient name, because "dispensed methadone to patient X" in a
//   compliance-readable table is itself a disclosure.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Where a prescription has got to in the dispensary — pharmacy's own state,
/// beside a clinical record it may not touch.
///
/// ⚠️ `NEW` IS NEVER STORED. A prescription with no fulfilment row IS new; the
///   row is created when somebody first acts on it. The member exists because
///   the QUEUE renders it and a screen that has to special-case "no row" in
///   three places will eventually forget one.
enum PrescriptionFulfilmentStatus {
  NEW
  /// A pharmacist has read it and confirmed it is dispensable. Step [6] of the
  /// flow in PHARMACY_ARCHITECTURE.md.
  VERIFIED
  PARTIALLY_DISPENSED
  COMPLETED
  /// The dispensary is not going to supply it — the patient went elsewhere, the
  /// prescriber withdrew it. ⚠️ NOT a cancellation OF the prescription, which
  /// is the prescriber's act and lives in the clinical record.
  CANCELLED
}

/// Was there a prescription behind this supply?
///
/// ⚠️ THERE IS NO `is_otc` ANYWHERE IN THIS PROGRAMME, AND THIS ENUM IS NOT ONE
///   IN DISGUISE. It records what HAPPENED — somebody presented a prescription,
///   or somebody bought something over the counter. Whether the product MAY be
///   supplied without a prescription is a per-jurisdiction question that only
///   `@rcln/regulatory` answers, and the same product is over-the-counter in one
///   country and prescription-only in the next.
enum DispenseKind {
  PRESCRIPTION
  COUNTER_SALE
  /// Ordered remotely and sent out (PI-12).
  ///
  /// ⚠️ ADDING THIS MEMBER RESTATES WHAT THE COLUMN ALWAYS WAS. The comment
  ///   above asks "was there a prescription behind this supply?", and that
  ///   question has always been answered by `encounter_id` being NULL or not —
  ///   `PRESCRIPTION` and `COUNTER_SALE` are a COUNTER's two ways of supplying,
  ///   which is a channel. `ONLINE` is the third, and an online supply may be
  ///   prescription-backed or not, which is why the CHECK constraint does not
  ///   tie it to an encounter.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ WHAT IT IS TIED TO IS A PATIENT. A parcel has to go to somebody, and a
  ///   supply nobody can attribute cannot be traced when its lot is recalled.
  ONLINE
}

enum DispenseStatus {
  DISPENSED
  PARTIALLY_RETURNED
  RETURNED
}

/// What happened to stock that came back.
///
/// ⚠️ THE DEFAULT IS `QUARANTINED` AND IT IS NOT A CONSERVATISM WE INVENTED.
///   Many jurisdictions forbid restocking a dispensed medicine outright: once it
///   has left the counter nobody can attest to how it was stored. Whether a
///   return may go back to `AVAILABLE` is a regulatory and clinic-policy
///   decision, so the engine is asked and the answer is recorded here.
enum DispenseReturnDisposition {
  RESTOCKED
  QUARANTINED
}

/// Pharmacy's workflow state over one consultation's prescription.
///
/// ⚠️ ONE ROW PER ENCOUNTER, NOT PER PRESCRIBED LINE. "The prescription" that a
///   patient carries to the counter is the whole medication list a consultation
///   produced; a pharmacist verifies the sheet, not each drug in isolation.
///   Per-line progress is derived from `dispense_lines`, which is where the
///   quantities actually are — storing a dispensed-so-far column here as well
///   would be a second answer to the same question, free to disagree.
///
/// ⚠️ IT IS CREATED LAZILY. A consultation that nobody dispenses against never
///   grows one, so the queue reads encounters and left-joins this; see
///   `queue.service.ts` for why that read is the shape it is.
model PrescriptionFulfilment {
  id             String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  organizationId String @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  /// ⚠️ THE BRANCH THAT IS DISPENSING, WHICH NEED NOT BE THE ONE THAT
  ///   PRESCRIBED. A group's patient may take a prescription written at the main
  ///   site to the satellite's dispensary, and the queue there has to show it.
  branchId       String @map("branch_id") @db.Uuid

  encounterId String @map("encounter_id") @db.Uuid

  status PrescriptionFulfilmentStatus @default(VERIFIED)

  verifiedById String?   @map("verified_by_id") @db.Uuid
  verifiedAt   DateTime? @map("verified_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  /// ⚠️ PHI. A pharmacist's note about this person's prescription — "rang the
  ///   prescriber about the dose". Free text, and treated as clinical.
  notes        String?   @db.Text

  cancelledById String?   @map("cancelled_by_id") @db.Uuid
  cancelledAt   DateTime? @map("cancelled_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  organization Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  branch       Branch       @relation(fields: [organizationId, branchId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  encounter    Encounter    @relation(fields: [organizationId, encounterId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)

  verifiedBy  User? @relation("PrescriptionFulfilmentVerifiedBy", fields: [verifiedById], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  cancelledBy User? @relation("PrescriptionFulfilmentCancelledBy", fields: [cancelledById], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)

  /// One dispensary state per consultation. ⚠️ Org-qualified, never bare — a
  /// `@@unique([encounterId])` on a tenant table is the mistake CLAUDE.md names.
  @@unique([organizationId, encounterId])
  @@unique([organizationId, id])
  /// The queue: what is outstanding at this counter, oldest first.
  @@index([organizationId, branchId, status, createdAt])
  @@map("prescription_fulfilments")
}

/// One supply of one or more products to one person, at one counter, at one
/// moment. The record of an irreversible physical act.
///
/// ⚠️ APPEND-ONLY IN SPIRIT AND MUTABLE IN EXACTLY ONE COLUMN. `status` moves as
///   returns come back, and nothing else on a posted dispense may be rewritten —
///   there is no update path in the service and no draft to amend. A dispense
///   made in error is corrected by a RETURN, which is another record, the same
///   way an invoice is corrected by a credit note and never by an edit.
model Dispense {
  id             String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  organizationId String @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  branchId       String @map("branch_id") @db.Uuid

  /// Issued from `number_sequences` (`DISPENSE`, per branch, never resets) INSIDE
  /// the posting transaction, so a refusal burns no number.
  dispenseNumber String @map("dispense_number") @db.VarChar(64)

  kind   DispenseKind
  status DispenseStatus @default(DISPENSED)

  /// The consultation whose prescription this supplies. NULL for a counter sale.
  encounterId String? @map("encounter_id") @db.Uuid
  /// ⚠️ PHI, AND NULLABLE FOR A REASON THAT IS NOT LAZINESS. A counter sale is
  ///   frequently to somebody who is not a patient of this clinic and never
  ///   becomes one; inventing a patient record to hold a paracetamol sale would
  ///   put a named person in the clinical system because they bought something.
  ///   Where a prescription is presented, this is NOT NULL — enforced by CHECK.
  patientId   String? @map("patient_id") @db.Uuid

  /// Which dispensing point it went out of. Branch-qualified.
  locationId String @map("location_id") @db.Uuid

  dispensedById String   @map("dispensed_by_id") @db.Uuid
  /// ⚠️ WHEN IT WAS HANDED OVER. Distinct from `created_at`, and it is what every
  ///   ledger leg carries as its `occurred_at`.
  dispensedAt   DateTime @default(now()) @map("dispensed_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  /// ⚠️ PHI. Anything the counter recorded about this supply.
  notes String? @db.Text

  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  organization Organization      @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  branch       Branch            @relation(fields: [organizationId, branchId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  encounter    Encounter?        @relation(fields: [organizationId, encounterId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict)
  /// Restrict, not Cascade: a person's dispensing history is a retention
  /// obligation in most jurisdictions and outlives their being a current patient.
  patient      Patient?          @relation(fields: [organizationId, patientId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict)
  location     InventoryLocation @relation("DispenseLocation", fields: [organizationId, branchId, locationId], references: [organizationId, branchId, id], onDelete: Restrict)
  dispensedBy  User              @relation("DispenseDispensedBy", fields: [dispensedById], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)

  lines   DispenseLine[]
  returns DispenseReturn[]
  /// The online order this supply fulfilled, where one did (PI-12). At most one,
  /// by `@@unique([organizationId, dispenseId])` on that side — see the header
  /// on `online-pharmacy.prisma` for why the foreign key lives there.
  onlineOrder OnlineOrder? @relation("OnlineOrderDispense")

  @@unique([organizationId, dispenseNumber])
  @@unique([organizationId, id])
  @@unique([organizationId, branchId, id])
  @@index([organizationId, branchId, dispensedAt(sort: Desc)])
  @@index([organizationId, encounterId])
  /// "What has this person been given" — a PHI read, and the index that makes it
  /// answerable in one scan.
  @@index([organizationId, patientId, dispensedAt(sort: Desc)])
  @@map("dispenses")
}

/// One product supplied on one dispense.
model DispenseLine {
  id             String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  organizationId String @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  branchId       String @map("branch_id") @db.Uuid
  dispenseId     String @map("dispense_id") @db.Uuid

  lineNumber Int @map("line_number") @db.SmallInt

  /// The prescribed line this answers. NULL on a counter sale, and NULL where a
  /// pharmacist supplies something the prescription did not list — which is a
  /// thing that happens and must be recordable as itself rather than forced into
  /// a prescription line it does not belong to.
  encounterPrescriptionId String? @map("encounter_prescription_id") @db.Uuid

  /// What was actually handed over.
  productId String @map("product_id") @db.Uuid
  /// What the prescriber wrote, where that is a DIFFERENT product.
  ///
  /// ⚠️ TWO INDEPENDENT QUESTIONS, AND CONFLATING THEM IS THE CLASSIC ERROR OF
  ///   THIS DOMAIN. "Is it equivalent?" is the composition triangle. "May I
  ///   substitute it?" is `@rcln/regulatory`, per jurisdiction and sometimes per
  ///   prescriber instruction. A product being equivalent does not make it
  ///   substitutable, and the default in the absence of a rule is DO NOT
  ///   (PI-ADR-007). This column records that a substitution was made; the
  ///   decision snapshot below records that it was allowed.
  substitutedForProductId String? @map("substituted_for_product_id") @db.Uuid
  /// Why. ⚠️ CHECKed present whenever a substitution was made.
  substitutionReason      String? @map("substitution_reason") @db.Text

  /// What the person typed, and the unit they thought in.
  quantityEntered Decimal @map("quantity_entered") @db.Decimal(18, 6)
  unitId          String  @map("unit_id") @db.Uuid
  /// The same amount in the product's base unit, converted through the one
  /// `toBaseUnits` the ledger uses. ⚠️ Positive here; the ledger leg carries the
  /// sign, and the sign is a property of `DISPENSING` rather than a choice.
  quantityBase    Decimal @map("quantity_base") @db.Decimal(18, 6)

  /// How much of this line has come back. Maintained by the return service and
  /// CHECKed at or below `quantity_base`.
  returnedQuantityBase Decimal @default(0) @map("returned_quantity_base") @db.Decimal(18, 6)

  /// ⚠️ THE SNAPSHOT THAT PERMITTED THIS, AND IT IS NOT NULLABLE (PI-ADR-008).
  ///   Every supplied line cites the decision made at the moment it was supplied.
  ///   Re-running the engine over a two-year-old dispense must never be necessary
  ///   and must never change what it says.
  regulatoryDecisionId String @map("regulatory_decision_id") @db.Uuid

  /// ⚠️ PHI. What goes on the label the patient reads — "one tablet twice a day
  ///   after food". Copied from the prescription at the moment of supply, because
  ///   the label is a statement about what was handed over and a later correction
  ///   to the prescription does not change what the box says.
  labelInstructions String? @map("label_instructions") @db.Text

  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  organization Organization  @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  branch       Branch        @relation(fields: [organizationId, branchId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  dispense     Dispense      @relation(fields: [organizationId, dispenseId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  /// Plain FKs into possibly-platform rows — `product_visible`, `unit_visible`.
  product      Product       @relation("DispenseLineProduct", fields: [productId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  substitutedForProduct Product? @relation("DispenseLineSubstitutedFor", fields: [substitutedForProductId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  unit         UnitOfMeasure @relation("DispenseLineUnit", fields: [unitId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)

  encounterPrescription EncounterPrescription? @relation(fields: [organizationId, encounterPrescriptionId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict)

  regulatoryDecision RegulatoryDecision @relation(fields: [organizationId, regulatoryDecisionId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict)

  allocations DispenseAllocation[]
  returnLines DispenseReturnLine[]
  /// The money side of this supply (PI-8). ⚠️ AT MOST ONE, enforced by a PARTIAL
  ///   unique index in the migration — the idempotency guarantee that stops a
  ///   retried post billing somebody twice. Pharmacy still owns no rate: this row
  ///   is a hand-off to the invoice engine and holds no tax figure.
  chargeRequests ChargeRequest[]

  @@unique([organizationId, dispenseId, lineNumber])
  @@unique([organizationId, id])
  @@unique([organizationId, branchId, id])
  @@index([organizationId, dispenseId])
  @@index([organizationId, productId])
  /// "How much of this prescribed line has been supplied" — the fulfilment
  /// arithmetic, and the reason PI-7 needed no column on the clinical record.
  @@index([organizationId, encounterPrescriptionId])
  @@map("dispense_lines")
}

/// Which physical lot the quantity on a line came out of.
///
/// ⚠️ ITS OWN TABLE RATHER THAN COLUMNS ON THE LINE, BECAUSE ONE LINE ROUTINELY
///   SPANS TWO LOTS. Thirty tablets where the oldest lot has eighteen left is an
///   ordinary FEFO outcome, and a `batch_id` on the line would force the
///   pharmacist to key two lines for one prescribed medicine — which then reads
///   as two supplies to every report and every fulfilment sum.
model DispenseAllocation {
  id             String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  organizationId String @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  branchId       String @map("branch_id") @db.Uuid
  dispenseLineId String @map("dispense_line_id") @db.Uuid

  locationId String  @map("location_id") @db.Uuid
  batchId    String? @map("batch_id") @db.Uuid
  serialId   String? @map("serial_id") @db.Uuid

  quantityBase Decimal @map("quantity_base") @db.Decimal(18, 6)

  /// Did a human overrule the FEFO plan for this lot?
  ///
  /// ⚠️ RECORDED, NOT PREVENTED, AND THE REASON IS REQUIRED WHEN IT IS TRUE. A
  ///   pharmacist has legitimate grounds to reach past the oldest lot — a
  ///   damaged strip, a patient's own supply being matched — and an allocation
  ///   that silently committed would leave "why did it give out the lot expiring
  ///   next week instead of the one expiring tomorrow" unanswerable.
  isOverride     Boolean @default(false) @map("is_override")
  overrideReason String? @map("override_reason") @db.Text

  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  organization Organization      @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  branch       Branch            @relation(fields: [organizationId, branchId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  dispenseLine DispenseLine      @relation(fields: [organizationId, dispenseLineId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  /// Branch-qualified, exactly as the ledger's are: an allocation at branch A
  /// citing a lot or a device at branch B is unrepresentable.
  location     InventoryLocation @relation("DispenseAllocationLocation", fields: [organizationId, branchId, locationId], references: [organizationId, branchId, id], onDelete: Restrict)
  batch        Batch?            @relation("DispenseAllocationBatch", fields: [organizationId, branchId, batchId], references: [organizationId, branchId, id], onDelete: Restrict)
  serial       Serial?           @relation("DispenseAllocationSerial", fields: [organizationId, branchId, serialId], references: [organizationId, branchId, id], onDelete: Restrict)

  returnLines DispenseReturnLine[]

  @@unique([organizationId, id])
  @@unique([organizationId, branchId, id])
  @@index([organizationId, dispenseLineId])
  /// Traceability: "which patients got this lot" is asked from the batch side,
  /// and PI-10's recall walks exactly this index.
  @@index([organizationId, batchId])
  @@index([organizationId, serialId])
  @@map("dispense_allocations")
}

/// Something came back.
///
/// ⚠️ A RETURN NEVER EDITS THE DISPENSE IT CITES. It is a `RETURN` ledger
///   movement plus this record, the same discipline the invoice engine applies
///   with a credit note — and financially it becomes one, in PI-8, through the
///   existing engine rather than by touching an invoice here.
model DispenseReturn {
  id             String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  organizationId String @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  branchId       String @map("branch_id") @db.Uuid

  dispenseId String @map("dispense_id") @db.Uuid

  /// Where it goes back to. See `DispenseReturnDisposition` — quarantine is the
  /// default and the engine is asked before anything is restocked.
  disposition DispenseReturnDisposition @default(QUARANTINED)

  /// Which shelf received it. Branch-qualified.
  locationId String @map("location_id") @db.Uuid

  /// ⚠️ PHI-adjacent: why a named person brought a medicine back.
  reason String @db.Text

  returnedAt   DateTime @default(now()) @map("returned_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  receivedById String   @map("received_by_id") @db.Uuid

  /// The decision that decided the disposition. Nullable, because a return of a
  /// product with no regulatory profile in an unconfigured jurisdiction is the
  /// ordinary case and `UNDETERMINED` there means "quarantine it", not "stop".
  regulatoryDecisionId String? @map("regulatory_decision_id") @db.Uuid

  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  organization Organization        @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  branch       Branch              @relation(fields: [organizationId, branchId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  dispense     Dispense            @relation(fields: [organizationId, dispenseId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict)
  location     InventoryLocation   @relation("DispenseReturnLocation", fields: [organizationId, branchId, locationId], references: [organizationId, branchId, id], onDelete: Restrict)
  receivedBy   User                @relation("DispenseReturnReceivedBy", fields: [receivedById], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict)
  regulatoryDecision RegulatoryDecision? @relation(fields: [organizationId, regulatoryDecisionId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict)

  lines DispenseReturnLine[]

  @@unique([organizationId, id])
  @@unique([organizationId, branchId, id])
  @@index([organizationId, dispenseId])
  @@index([organizationId, branchId, returnedAt(sort: Desc)])
  @@map("dispense_returns")
}

/// One lot's worth of one line, coming back.
model DispenseReturnLine {
  id               String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  organizationId   String @map("organization_id") @db.Uuid
  branchId         String @map("branch_id") @db.Uuid
  dispenseReturnId String @map("dispense_return_id") @db.Uuid

  dispenseLineId String @map("dispense_line_id") @db.Uuid
  /// The allocation it came out of, so the lot it goes back INTO is the lot it
  /// came OUT of rather than whichever one is oldest. ⚠️ Returning a lot to the
  /// wrong bucket makes a recall miss the units it went looking for.
  dispenseAllocationId String? @map("dispense_allocation_id") @db.Uuid

  quantityBase Decimal @map("quantity_base") @db.Decimal(18, 6)

  createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz(6)

  organization Organization        @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  branch       Branch              @relation(fields: [organizationId, branchId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  dispenseReturn DispenseReturn    @relation(fields: [organizationId, dispenseReturnId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Cascade)
  dispenseLine DispenseLine        @relation(fields: [organizationId, dispenseLineId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict)
  dispenseAllocation DispenseAllocation? @relation(fields: [organizationId, dispenseAllocationId], references: [organizationId, id], onDelete: Restrict)
  /// The money side of this return (PI-8) — a `REVERSAL` charge request, which
  /// cancels an unbilled charge or becomes a credit note against a billed one.
  chargeRequests     ChargeRequest[]

  @@unique([organizationId, id])
  @@index([organizationId, dispenseReturnId])
  @@index([organizationId, dispenseLineId])
  @@map("dispense_return_lines")
}
